WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.971
A Disjoint Set Union maintains a collection of non-overlapping sets under dynamic edge additions.

00:00:06.971 --> 00:00:12.146
Each component forms a directed tree rooted at a representative element.

00:00:12.146 --> 00:00:17.320
Two nodes belong to the same component if and only if they share a root.

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:24.240
During a find operation, redirect every visited node on the path so it points directly to the root.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.910
Path compression flattens tall chains into broad stars.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.913
Future queries on those nodes finish in almost a single hop.

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:38.415
When merging two roots, attach the smaller tree underneath the root of the larger tree.

00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:43.175
Union by size keeps tree depth logarithmic even before compression.

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:48.433
Combined with path compression, operations run in amortized constant time.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:56.742
Store extra metadata such as component size, minimum element, or parity at each root and merge it during union.

00:00:56.742 --> 00:01:03.137
When a problem deletes edges, process the operations in reverse order as edge insertions.

00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:07.018
DSU turns dynamic connectivity into fast root lookups.
